<title>HONG KONG: H.K. dlr July M-3 rises 12.3 pct on year.</title>
<headline>H.K. dlr July M-3 rises 12.3 pct on year.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Hong Kong Monetary Authority gave the following money supply figures as percentage changes:</p>
<p>				   July '96    June '96   July '95</p>
<p> HK dollar M-3 (year-on-year)  +12.3	 +13.2	+18.6</p>
<p> HK dollar M-3 (month)	    +0.9	  +2.5	 +1.7</p>
<p>				   July '96    June '96   July '95</p>
<p> HK dollar M-1 (year-on-year)   +6.9	  +5.1	 +4.2</p>
<p> HK dollar M-1 (month)	    +1.9	  +2.2	 +0.3</p>
<p> HK dollar M-2 (year-on-year)  +12.7	 +13.5	+18.8</p>
<p> HK dollar M-2 (month)	    +1.0	  +2.5	 +1.7</p>
<p>Loans to finance visible trade of Hong Kong (year-on-Year)</p>
<p>				     +6.1	  +7.5	 +28.1</p>
<p>Other loans for use in Hong Kong (year-on-year)</p>
<p>				    +14.2	 +14.2	 +12.9</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441 No text received</p>
</text>
